1
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:15,432
<i>It was a miracle.</i>

2
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:17,642
<i>Yes, it would go down in the history of Mars</i>

4
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:22,188
<i>as The 7-minute Miracle.</i>

5
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:24,441
<i>This is the story</i>

6
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:26,484
<i>of the two girls</i>

7
00:00:27,068 --> 00:00:29,654
<i>who were the driving force behind it.</i>

8
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:03,873
<i>I can't believe it!</i>

9
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:05,041
<i>Life has been crazy</i>

10
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:09,044
<i>ever since I met Tuesday a few months ago</i>
<i>after she ran away from home.</i>

11
00:02:09,503 --> 00:02:11,881
<i>After playing for an audience of ten</i>
<i>at our first concert,</i>

12
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:16,052
<i>and in front of 100,000</i>
<i>at the Cydonia Festival, we met Crystal.</i>

13
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:18,513
<i>That's crazy.</i>

14
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:21,683
<i>Crystal smelled so good!</i>

15
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:31,317
I've been blind the whole time.

16
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:34,237
People never notice the obvious.

17
00:02:35,572 --> 00:02:36,406
What is it?

18
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:39,200
Why didn't I notice it until now?

19
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:40,577
What do you mean?

20
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:43,037
A shortcut to your debut.

21
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:45,248
It was right in front of us
the whole time.

22
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:46,416
What do you mean?

23
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:49,085
It's kind of old-school.

24
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:52,463
I see! An audition show!

25
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:55,049
Mars Brightest!

26
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:57,260
<i>Passionate performances!</i>

27
00:02:57,927 --> 00:02:58,803
<i>Exciting concerts!</i>

28
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:00,805
<i>Sparkling voices!</i>

29
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:04,767
<i>Performers with God-given talents gather</i>

30
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,811
<i>to compete for their debut.</i>

31
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:09,814
<i>That's </i>"Mars Brightest"!

32
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,692
<i>The next brightest star</i>

33
00:03:13,151 --> 00:03:13,985
<i>is you!</i>

34
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:23,953
If you win on this show,

35
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:25,538
you get to make your debut.

36
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:28,917
Most performers that make their debut
through the show become chart-toppers.

37
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,835
Haven't you seen it before?

38
00:03:31,210 --> 00:03:32,295
You guys

39
00:03:32,795 --> 00:03:36,382
are going to go on the show, win big,
and make your grand debut!

40
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:38,009
It's not that easy.

41
00:03:38,343 --> 00:03:40,345
I'll go ahead and apply.

42
00:03:40,428 --> 00:03:41,721
What? Wait!

43
00:03:42,096 --> 00:03:44,057
Tell me your height, weight,

44
00:03:44,224 --> 00:03:46,476
and bust, waist, and hip measurements.

45
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:48,686
What? That's sexual harassment.

46
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:51,272
No! That's what it says
on the application!

47
00:03:51,522 --> 00:03:52,357
Really?

48
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,943
Just write something. Let me see that.

49
00:03:55,401 --> 00:04:02,033
-Height: 129. Weight: 129. Bust size: 129.
-Stop!

50
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:03,910
I submitted it.

51
00:04:05,119 --> 00:04:06,788
You're horrible.

52
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:08,957
First, it's the local competition.

53
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:12,126
By the way, 200,000 people
applied last year.

54
00:04:12,585 --> 00:04:14,420
-What?
-Two hundred thousand?

55
00:04:14,587 --> 00:04:18,507
Only eight groups get selected
to appear on the show.

56
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:24,264
Anyway, just focus on writing songs
and rehearsing.

57
00:04:24,681 --> 00:04:27,433
I want to, but I'm broke.

58
00:04:27,642 --> 00:04:28,935
I have to work.

59
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:31,354
You don't have to work anymore.

60
00:04:32,021 --> 00:04:34,107
You got paid for performing at Cydonia.

61
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:36,401
But we only played one song!

62
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:40,196
980 Oolongs after taxes
and miscellaneous fees.

63
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,114
That's nothing.

64
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:42,782
We got paid!

65
00:04:43,283 --> 00:04:44,826
I feel like we're pros now.

66
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:45,952
We did it!

67
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:47,245
Anyway,

68
00:04:47,620 --> 00:04:49,372
I'll hold on to it for now.

69
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:51,666
-What?
-I won't do anything bad.

70
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:54,502
I have a bad feeling about this.

71
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:59,007
<i>You keep too many secrets.</i>

72
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:03,970
I understand you're powerful enough
to get Intergalactic to invest in you.

73
00:05:04,929 --> 00:05:08,516
However, we have no idea
what's next in your plan.

74
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:12,437
You have to be more open
with your information.

75
00:05:12,812 --> 00:05:15,606
When and where am I supposed to sing?

76
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,027
<i>-Mars Brightest.</i>
-What?

77
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,446
You're going to go on that show.

78
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:25,074
You got them to invest 12 million,

79
00:05:25,158 --> 00:05:28,328
and now you're putting her
on an audition show?

80
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:32,665
Why does my Angela have to compete
against amateurs?

81
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:37,503
Angela is already famous, so it would be
unusual for her to compete in the show.

82
00:05:38,254 --> 00:05:40,715
However, the show will bring publicity.

83
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:44,469
Competing out in the open
and winning with raw talent

84
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:47,138
is an effective method
for building your brand

85
00:05:47,513 --> 00:05:49,849
as a singer.

86
00:05:50,433 --> 00:05:51,267
However,

87
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,644
there is no need to compete
in the local competitions.

88
00:05:53,978 --> 00:05:55,146
You'll appear in the main show

89
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:57,607
as part of a special category.

90
00:05:58,316 --> 00:06:01,819
Has it already been decided
that Angela's going to win?

91
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:03,863
The viewers aren't stupid.

92
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,823
They'd find out if that happened.

93
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:08,951
But what if she loses to an amateur?

94
00:06:11,662 --> 00:06:13,956
Are you going to lose to an amateur?

95
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:17,251
Who are you talking to?

96
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:26,302
We're here at the Alba City venue
on <i>Mars Brightest.</i>

97
00:06:26,677 --> 00:06:28,930
It's totally packed!

98
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:31,265
Will one of today's contestants

99
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:34,644
turn out to be Mars' brightest star?

100
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:36,729
I can't wait!

101
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:39,565
They're all rivals.

102
00:06:40,650 --> 00:06:43,152
You have to win against all of them.

103
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:45,988
Is this really a shortcut?

104
00:06:57,834 --> 00:06:58,751
Hi!

105
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,337
All my followers on Mars,
are you watching this?

106
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:07,135
I'm in
the <i>Mars Brightest</i> preliminaries today!

107
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,386
I'm so excited!

108
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:12,348
Look, look. There's lots of weirdoes here.

109
00:07:12,515 --> 00:07:15,101
Oh, no! I should have worn more makeup!

110
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:16,978
I look frumpy.

111
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:19,564
Hey, I found someone who looks even
frumpier than me.

112
00:07:20,022 --> 00:07:21,899
Hey! Are you guys competing, too?

113
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:23,651
Who are you?

114
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:26,946
Don't you know who I am? I'm so shocked!

115
00:07:27,029 --> 00:07:28,990
So, I'm not famous yet?

116
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:30,450
Isn't that Pyotr?

117
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:32,326
Pyotr from Instagram.

118
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,788
There's a social media star here!

119
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:38,749
Pyotr's here, too!
Pyotr's popular among female fans.

120
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:43,296
Great. So, I am sort of famous?

121
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,964
A few words, please!

122
00:07:46,132 --> 00:07:49,469
I'm going to do my best to win
and become even more famous!

123
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,930
By the way, Tuesday,
you ran away from home, right?

124
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:55,516
Are you okay with being photographed?

125
00:07:57,101 --> 00:07:59,187
You guys, it's almost your turn.

126
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:00,980
Oh, no!

127
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:02,607
Just make sure no one recognizes you.

128
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,567
Recognizes you? What do you mean?

129
00:08:04,984 --> 00:08:06,486
It's complicated.

130
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:07,737
What am I going to do?

131
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:09,655
Come on.

132
00:08:09,906 --> 00:08:11,240
It can't be helped.

133
00:08:13,117 --> 00:08:15,077
Hey. I'm going to borrow these for a bit.

134
00:08:15,453 --> 00:08:17,455
-Hey!
-I'll give them back later.

135
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:20,458
So? Can you recognize me?

136
00:08:21,959 --> 00:08:23,002
It'll work.

137
00:09:00,414 --> 00:09:02,208
I'm Idea, the AI singer.

138
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:06,254
I'm a high-performance AI
designed to sing!

139
00:09:06,712 --> 00:09:08,464
My hobby is charging.

140
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:28,693
I'm Charlotte. I'm 7 years old.

141
00:09:29,068 --> 00:09:30,444
I'll do my best to sing today.

142
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:16,866
My mother passed away recently.

143
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,828
My mother used to like to sing this song.

144
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:41,474
I'm a native Martian.

145
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:44,852
I'm going to sing in the Martian language.

146
00:11:03,079 --> 00:11:04,830
Hi. What are your names?

147
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:06,540
Carole and...

148
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:10,252
Monday.

149
00:11:11,629 --> 00:11:14,382
It says "Tuesday"
on your application form.

150
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:16,634
Which is it?

151
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:22,264
Sometimes I'm Monday, and also Wednesday.

152
00:11:22,431 --> 00:11:25,017
Never mind. Where are you from?

153
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:30,523
Well... I don't speak Martian very well.

154
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:31,941
I see...

155
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:33,943
Can you speak Martian, Carole?

156
00:11:34,819 --> 00:11:38,989
Yes. I'm from Earth,
but I lived in a refugee camp.

157
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:41,951
I moved to Mars when I was a kid.

158
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:44,203
So, I don't remember much about Earth.

159
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,872
Then do you live with your family now?

160
00:11:47,164 --> 00:11:50,292
No. My parents have been gone
since I can remember.

161
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:53,295
I heard they abandoned me at a church.

162
00:11:54,171 --> 00:11:55,005
I see.

163
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:57,383
That must have been hard.

164
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,385
I guess.

165
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:02,054
I always thought it was normal.

166
00:12:03,722 --> 00:12:06,183
Can you play your song for us?

167
00:12:06,725 --> 00:12:07,560
Are you ready?

168
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:14,316
Please listen.

169
00:12:30,040 --> 00:12:32,793
The new manager will be coming next week.

170
00:12:34,753 --> 00:12:35,838
Angie.

171
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:39,216
There's not much time left
until <i>Mars Brightest.</i>

172
00:12:40,092 --> 00:12:42,052
Why don't you come back home?

173
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:45,556
I've kept your room the way it was.

174
00:12:45,848 --> 00:12:48,392
Seeing you living on your own
makes me worried.

175
00:12:50,644 --> 00:12:52,271
I won't do things like that anymore.

176
00:12:52,855 --> 00:12:55,316
It happened because of the medicine's
side effects.

177
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:58,235
I'm stable now.

178
00:13:00,696 --> 00:13:02,740
-Angie.
-Mom.

179
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:05,409
I'm fine on my own.

180
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:07,828
Don't worry.

181
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:12,458
You can come back home anytime.

182
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:20,049
<i>Mom, sorry.</i>

183
00:13:21,008 --> 00:13:21,842
<i>I can't go back.</i>

184
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:27,139
<i>The bedcovers I've been using</i>
<i>since I was a kid...</i>

185
00:13:28,682 --> 00:13:30,643
<i>The ugly curtain pattern...</i>

186
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:34,855
<i>The stains on the wall...</i>

187
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:38,609
<i>The trophies I won</i>
<i>while I was a child actor...</i>

188
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:42,446
<i>The sound of my mom's voice</i>
<i>when she's mad...</i>

189
00:13:43,197 --> 00:13:44,031
<i>Her hands...</i>

190
00:13:45,115 --> 00:13:46,200
<i>When I'm there...</i>

191
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,619
<i>I feel like I'm suffocating.</i>

192
00:13:50,329 --> 00:13:51,163
Angela!

193
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:53,999
Angela! Angela! Angela!

194
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:55,793
Leave me alone.

195
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:27,575
-Hey.
-Roddy?

196
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:28,951
Hi.

197
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:31,078
What? Were you waiting for us?

198
00:14:31,453 --> 00:14:32,705
You stalker!

199
00:14:33,247 --> 00:14:34,081
No!

200
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,542
I was just in the area for work.

201
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:38,085
Really?

202
00:14:38,544 --> 00:14:40,337
How was the audition?

203
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:42,965
I was so nervous!

204
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:44,550
When will you know the results?

205
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,177
They'll tell you in about a week.

206
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:48,554
Think you passed?

207
00:14:48,637 --> 00:14:50,097
Who knows.

208
00:14:50,389 --> 00:14:52,683
What? Have confidence in yourself!

209
00:14:53,058 --> 00:14:54,852
I scouted you guys!

210
00:14:55,102 --> 00:14:57,730
That's right! Gus can be weird,

211
00:14:57,813 --> 00:14:59,481
but he knows talent when he sees it.

212
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:00,983
Hey. Weird?

213
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:01,984
I mean...

214
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:04,028
-Weird? You know, weird.
-Yeah, weird.

215
00:15:04,111 --> 00:15:04,945
Yeah.

216
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,452
Tuesday, there you are.

217
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:54,870
What's wrong?

218
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:57,039
You're acting weird these days.

219
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:00,793
I came to this city

220
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:03,629
without a plan.

221
00:16:05,172 --> 00:16:07,216
You helped me a lot.

222
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:09,385
But...

223
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:13,263
I still don't know anything about you.

224
00:16:14,556 --> 00:16:15,933
I was always thinking about myself,

225
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:17,476
like how I ran away from home,

226
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,436
and don't want anyone to find me.

227
00:16:20,521 --> 00:16:22,147
I was always thinking about my secrets.

228
00:16:22,982 --> 00:16:24,358
I'm always hesitating.

229
00:16:25,401 --> 00:16:26,568
And I don't have confidence.

230
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,738
I'm disappointed in myself.

231
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:34,910
I envy you, Carole.

232
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:38,038
I wish I could be you, Carole.

233
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:42,167
I get overwhelmed

234
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:45,004
by my own problems sometimes, too.

235
00:16:45,921 --> 00:16:48,340
I don't open up to just anyone.

236
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:50,884
I can tell you what I really think

237
00:16:51,301 --> 00:16:52,553
because of who you are, Tuesday.

238
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:57,641
And when you're singing,
you look like you're having fun.

239
00:16:58,142 --> 00:16:59,685
You come alive.

240
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:02,813
Maybe you don't notice it yourself,
though.

241
00:17:06,066 --> 00:17:07,276
Hey, Carole.

242
00:17:08,484 --> 00:17:09,319
I don't have

243
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:12,196
many memories of my father either.

244
00:17:13,031 --> 00:17:15,409
My parents divorced when I was small.

245
00:17:15,951 --> 00:17:17,327
I haven't seen him for a long time.

246
00:17:18,078 --> 00:17:18,912
Yeah.

247
00:17:19,579 --> 00:17:21,665
My mom is a politician.

248
00:17:21,957 --> 00:17:23,541
No way! That's terrible!

249
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:24,835
It is terrible!

250
00:17:25,752 --> 00:17:27,880
By the way, my brother goes to Harvard.

251
00:17:28,255 --> 00:17:29,965
Wow, he's one of the elite!

252
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:31,341
Yes.

253
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:34,762
And I'm a loser who couldn't even
go to school anymore.

254
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,767
I didn't want to hide it from you, Carole.

255
00:17:40,726 --> 00:17:41,560
Yeah.

256
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,148
I hope we make it to the final round.

257
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:52,446
"Tuesday, how do you feel now?"

258
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:54,615
What?

259
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:57,034
We're practicing for when we win.

260
00:17:57,659 --> 00:17:59,036
How do you feel?

261
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:01,997
Well... So...

262
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:04,917
Actually, I knew we'd win.

263
00:18:06,210 --> 00:18:08,087
Considering our talents,

264
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,172
well, it's only natural!

265
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:23,227
Hey, instead of saying something,

266
00:18:23,352 --> 00:18:25,145
how about answering with a cool sign?

267
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:26,105
A sign?

268
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:29,233
Like what rappers do.

269
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:31,693
Like this?

270
00:18:32,986 --> 00:18:33,946
Maybe like this.

271
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:37,658
Hey, hey. Come on!

272
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:39,409
Hey.

273
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:41,662
Here.

274
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:43,080
There.

275
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:44,581
Like this!

276
00:18:51,171 --> 00:18:54,216
With all this practice,
I'd feel stupid if we lost.

277
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:57,845
-Carole.
-Yeah?

278
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,681
I'm not going to be afraid

279
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:02,266
of being recognized anymore.

280
00:19:04,434 --> 00:19:07,604
I'm here because
I want to make music with you.

281
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:10,816
I'm not doing anything wrong.

282
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:12,693
I want to be bold about it.

283
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:15,195
Yeah.

284
00:19:15,737 --> 00:19:16,738
What are you going to do

285
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:19,741
if your scary politician mom finds out?

286
00:19:20,284 --> 00:19:22,077
Well, when it comes to it...

287
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,496
whatever happens, happens!

288
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:26,582
Like a real tough guy!

289
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,006
All right.

290
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:36,383
I have some good news and some bad news.

291
00:19:36,717 --> 00:19:37,759
What should I start with?

292
00:19:39,803 --> 00:19:41,680
-What do you think?
-I'll be shocked if we lost.

293
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:43,932
But don't you want to know
the results first?

294
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,018
All right.

295
00:19:46,935 --> 00:19:48,478
The bad news first.

296
00:19:48,687 --> 00:19:49,688
Please.

297
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,648
You guys are going to

298
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:54,067
have to work again.

299
00:19:54,484 --> 00:19:55,319
What?

300
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,988
Your payment for the Cydonia Festival,

301
00:19:58,071 --> 00:19:59,948
980 Oolongs, is all gone.

302
00:20:01,825 --> 00:20:05,204
I wanted to grow the money
for funding your activities.

303
00:20:05,787 --> 00:20:08,040
But the dog wouldn't run!

304
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:09,833
Hold on. What did you do?

305
00:20:11,126 --> 00:20:13,003
I lost it all betting in a dog race.

306
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:17,299
-No way!
-That's not funny!

307
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,219
The good news next.

308
00:20:21,136 --> 00:20:22,262
To tell you the truth...

309
00:20:25,474 --> 00:20:27,726
I heard about it! You passed the
<i>Mars Brightest</i> prelims!

310
00:20:28,810 --> 00:20:29,645
What?

311
00:20:29,895 --> 00:20:31,730
You're one of the eight finalists!

312
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:34,316
-No way.
-Really?

313
00:20:34,608 --> 00:20:36,193
Roddy!

314
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,527
We did it!

315
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:41,573
I was just about to say that!

316
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:42,991
Sorry.

317
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:47,496
It's the TV station!

318
00:20:48,038 --> 00:20:48,872
No way!

319
00:20:49,164 --> 00:20:49,998
They're here already?

320
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:53,835
Hey, wait.

321
00:20:54,544 --> 00:20:55,629
Your sunglasses!

322
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:57,756
I don't need them anymore.

323
00:21:01,176 --> 00:21:03,512
Congratulations on making it
to the final round!

324
00:21:04,054 --> 00:21:05,430
How does it feel to have won

325
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:08,976
out of 200,000 contestants?

326
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:25,784
Yeah.

327
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:54,998
Subtitle translation by Hoday Stearns

